{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Xcode-asks-to-Trust--Enable-a-macro","text":"Xcode asks to “Trust & Enable” a macro","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are compiler plugins, so the first build in Xcode","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prompts once per machine to trust the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target. Approve it in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"build error’s fix-it or under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Settings → Packages","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". On CI, pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-skipMacroValidation"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — there’s no one to click the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dialog."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow","text":"The first build is slow","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift-syntax"},{"type":"text","text":", which the macro system compiles from source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".build\/"},{"text":" or DerivedData.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring","type":"heading","text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Something called ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":", or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"dispatched from an "},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context","text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift 6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"code":"nonisolated init","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation","text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"var flag = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write ","type":"text"},{"code":"var flag: Bool = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applies to combined declarations: split "},{"code":"var a, b: Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into separate"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"declarations."}]},{"anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" without a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"data-protection keychain never prompts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is persisted, but nothing crashes either: the write logs, returns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the app continues. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to get real persistence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Adding a team-prefixed "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement also works, and is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the right call when you want the access group — but weigh it first, because it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"makes the app require a provisioning profile for every signed build. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" a fix for a test host: ","type":"text"},{"code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" embeds no entitlements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at all, so there is nothing for the entitlement to attach to. Let the write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degrade there. Details in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Test-crashed-with-signal-trap-before-establishing-connection","text":"`Test crashed with signal trap before establishing connection`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"xcodebuild test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dies before any test runs, naming nothing useful. If the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mints a device identity or writes a token at launch, suspect the Keychain: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"test host is unsigned, the write fails, and a trap takes the process down before"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the test bundle can attach."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Current versions degrade instead of trapping here, so upgrading Swidux is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fix. To confirm the diagnosis on an older one, run the same scheme with"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — if it gets past launch, the Keychain was the cause."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Edits-disappear-after-a-sync-tick-or-an-async-load","text":"Edits disappear after a sync tick or an async load"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symptom: a keystroke, a toggle, or a whole entity vanishes — intermittently,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually while something is loading or syncing, and never reproducibly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The cause is almost always a hand-rolled bridge from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" work into the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"store. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":" keeps state in an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" observer tree and converts to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-type snapshot on the way in and out (“pack” and “unpack”). If you pack a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" something, and then unpack it, everything dispatched during","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" is silently overwritten:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var snapshot = AppState(observer: store.observer)   \/\/ ← packed BEFORE the await","await loadEverything(into: &snapshot)               \/\/ ← dispatches land here…","AppState.apply(snapshot, to: store.observer)        \/\/ ← …and are discarded here"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" across a suspension point is the tell. The window is only as wide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why it presents as a rare glitch rather than a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reproducible bug."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead. It runs the async work with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access to state, then packs a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"fresh","type":"text"}]},{"text":" snapshot, merges, and unpacks in a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"step with no suspension point in between — so no dispatch can interleave:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await store.mutate {","    try await api.fetchItems()          \/\/ no state in scope; nothing to stale","} merging: { items, state in","    state.items.merge(from: EntityStore(items)) { _, _ in false }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The persistence stack’s own async entry points already work this way — use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistence.rehydrate(into: store)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sync.setSyncEnabled(_:into: store)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a snapshot you manage yourself. (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hydrate(into: &state)"},{"text":" is the exception,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and safe: it runs at launch, before the store exists.)","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"gitignored "},{"code":".dev-tooling","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"already built without it, run "},{"code":"swift package purge-cache","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so SwiftPM re-reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the manifest. See the repository’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CONTRIBUTING.md"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#Predicate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a protocol-required keypath traps under ","type":"text"},{"code":"-O","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the macro generates a per-model "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiduxBatchFetchDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":". Run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"swift test -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in CI to catch this class of issue — Debug builds and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pass.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/mutate(awaiting:merging:)":{"title":"mutate(awaiting:merging:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mutate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"awaiting","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"merging","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs async work that must not hold state across its suspensions, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"folds the result into a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"freshly packed","type":"text"}]},{"text":" snapshot in one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"suspension-free step.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Swidux